# ── WALLET INTELLIGENCE (Sprint 65) — the wallets find US ──────────────────────
# The token flow already surfaces the top holders of every token we scan. Instead of
# hunting for a good wallet to follow (what everyone does), we let recurrence surface
# the wallets that keep showing up across the tokens we already analyze. Three tiers:
#   wallet_scan   — every top-holder wallet we've seen once. The raw net. Huge, bounded.
#   wallet_matched — a wallet seen 2+ times. Graduates out of scan, gets a tally, and
#                    is where TRACKING begins (the agent can name it, we compute its PnL).
#   (actively tracked lives inside wallet_matched via a "tracking" block once promoted)
# DOCTRINE: every number here is DATA TO REASON WITH, never a directive. A wallet
# selling is not "sell". A low hold time is not "bad token". The goal is to make money;
# these are inputs to the agent's judgment, not signals to obey.
# The SOL/stable legs of a swap — NOT tradeable memecoins. When parsing a wallet's
# swaps, these appearing as the "received/sent token" is the OTHER side of the trade
# (the money leg), not a position. Counting them as tokens poisons PnL (fake round
# trips, absurd % — this is the bug the first live test caught).
