# ─── THE GORK STANDARD (the agent's hold-score rubric) ───
# $GORK (76ED...pump) is the 10/10. Every hold is measured against it.
#
# The rubric is stored HERE, as a fixed reference, rather than re-derived from memory
# each time. A rubric that lives only in a prompt drifts: the same token scored twice
# gets two answers, and you can never tell whether the score changed or the scorer did.
# Fixed rubric, fixed criteria, scores comparable across months.
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING LAW: C1 (time under fire), C2 (red-tape output), C4 (origin
# integrity). Fail any one and NOTHING ELSE SAVES IT. High C5-C10 cannot rescue a
# C1/C2/C4 fail — that is precisely how cabals cosplay culture: ship the lore, buy the
