# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#                  SPRINT 32: MEETING FILES TUNABLE SCHEMA
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# TUNABLE_PARAMS defines every parameter the agent/the owner can override via plain-
# language directives in sniper_meeting.json. The local LLM (qwen3) reads a
# directive and matches it against this schema to produce structured changes.
#
# Each entry has:
#   type:        "int" | "float" | "bool" | "usd"
#   min/max:     hard bounds. LLM cannot output values outside these.
#   default:     the value if no override is active.
#   unit:        for human readability in audit logs.
#   description: what the parameter does. LLM uses this to match directives.
#
# HARD LOCKS (NOT in this schema, NEVER tunable via meetings):
#   NOTE the membership test is THIS DICT, not this comment. A name that
#   appears in TUNABLE_PARAMS is tunable no matter what any comment says.
#   FIX 7 (2026-08-15): WALLET_FLOOR_SOL was listed here as "hardcoded at
#   0.05" while sitting in the schema below and resolving through
#   get_override_sync at all six read sites. The immovable part is that a
#   floor EXISTS at all (sells must always be fundable); the NUMBER is a
#   knob. Delisted from the sermon so a meeting that raises the floor gets
#   applied or clarified, never bounced as HARD-LOCKED.
#   - BONDED_DEXIDS_ALLOWED       v13.0: graduated-DEX whitelist, hardcoded
#   - _LEDGER_SWEEP_*             wallet protection, code_tuner only
#   - SIGNAL_POLL_INTERVAL_S      agent signal poll, must stay fast
#   - POSITION_TICK_*             position monitor, must stay fast
#   - CA_RES_TICK_S               research responder depends on this cadence
#   - AUTOPSY_TICK_S              post-trade learning, must run
#   - WALLET_TICK_S               wallet snapshot dependencies
#   - ALL FILE PATHS              workspace structure
#   - ALL API ENDPOINTS           tool contracts
#   - ALL CREDENTIALS             security
#   - DEEP_RESEARCH_DEDUP_MINUTES anti-spam guard
#   - DEEP_RESEARCH_CACHE_TTL_*   cache integrity
#   - PATTERN_CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD pattern engine integrity
#   - MCAP_DROP_BLOCK_PCT         safety check
#   - RUGCHECK_FLIP_LOOKBACK_MIN  safety check
#   - SIZE_CAP_HYSTERESIS_FRAC    sizing guard
#   - MINT_COOLDOWN_HOURS         conflict prevention
